dow Authority Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Executive","time":"7.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Partner, Shareholder and Trustee Executive Sub-Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Reigate and Banstead forecasts \u00a3878k revenue overspend as industrial site sits vacant","lead":"Reigate and Banstead Council is projecting a \u00a3878k overspend for 2026/27, nearly four per cent above its \u00a323.6m budget, driven almost entirely by property income shortfalls. The Redhill Distribution Centre, a council-owned site of six industrial units, has remained empty through the first quarter and is generating a \u00a31,054k deficit from lost rental income. The council is actively marketing the site regionally and nationally and expects September and October to be key periods for lettings, though agents are drawing up terms for only a single unit following recent interest. Offsetting the property problems, underlying council services are tracking one-and-a-half per cent below budget, and the Environmental Licensing service is delivering a \u00a3257k underspend from higher-than-expected private hire vehicle licence income. The council has adequate reserves to manage the shortfall.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Annex 1.1 for Q1 Revenue and Capital Budget Monitoring 2026/27","paper_url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s43426/43426.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Reigate and Banstead forecasts \u00a3878k revenue overspend driven by vacant industrial units","lead":"Reigate and Banstead is forecasting a revenue overspend of \u00a3878k for 2026/27, roughly 3.7 per cent above budget, but the shortfall is almost entirely due to losses from council-owned property rather than overspending on services. Redhill Distribution Centre, which has remained vacant through the first quarter, accounts for \u00a31,054k of the overspend through lost rental income on its six industrial units and is being actively marketed regionally and nationally. When property income is excluded, the council's core services show a \u00a3382k underspend, indicating day-to-day spending is tracking ahead of budget. The overspend is partially offset by higher-than-expected income from private hire vehicle licences, which is delivering a \u00a3257k underspend in environmental licensing.","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Annex 1.1 for Q1 Revenue and Capital Budget Monitoring 2026/27","paper_url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s43426/43426.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"O&amp;S Minute 28 Q1 Performance 2026-27","paper_url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s43581/43581.pdf","headline":"Key projects workstream downgraded to Amber in LGR programme","detail":"One of four Local Government Reorganisation programme workstreams\u2014Key projects/chunky business delivery\u2014is now reporting Amber status, indicating deterioration from previous standing. Three workstreams continue to report Green. Expenditure remains within agreed budgets.","category":"governance","matters":"Deteriorating status on critical LGR preparation activity suggests potential delays in restructuring planning, which could have knock-on effects on service delivery and the council's financial position during transition.","figures":"1 of 4 workstreams Amber; 3 Green; expenditure within budgets","quote":"Three of the four programme workstreams continue to report as Green, while the Key projects/chunky business delivery workstream is now Amber.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"O&amp;S Minute 28 Q1 Performance 2026-27","paper_url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s43581/43581.pdf","headline":"Council preparing for closedown activity in advance of Local Government Reorganisation Vesting Day","detail":"From August 2026, council is introducing a new workstream focused on closedown activity. The council has structured its internal work around the need to mitigate the strategic risk that LGR presents to delivery of corporate objectives in the period before Vesting Day.","category":"governance","matters":"A council in closedown ahead of restructuring faces distinct risks to service continuity and financial stability; lenders need visibility of LGR timeline and any financial implications.","figures":"Closedown workstream commencing August 2026","quote":"From August onward a new workstream will be introduced, focusing on Council closedown activity; and the dashboard will therefore provide Members with an update on that in the future.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Addendum - OS Minute Q1 Revenue and Capital Budget 2026-27","paper_url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s43592/43592.pdf","headline":"Council projects a revenue overspend of approximately \u00a3878k by end of Q1 2026/27, primarily driven by loss of rental income from the vacant Redhill Distribution Centre.","detail":"Service budgets are forecasted to overspend by \u00a3906k, offset partially by a central budget underspend of \u00a328k, resulting in a net projected overspend of approximately \u00a3878k for the year. The root cause is loss of rental income from the vacant Redhill Distribution Centre. The Property team is actively seeking new tenants to recover this income.","category":"overspend","matters":"A material in-year revenue overspend of this scale requires either recovery action, spending controls, or reserve drawdown to balance the budget\u2014concerns that would be material to a lender assessing the council's financial control and reserves position.","figures":"\u00a3878k, \u00a3906k forecasted overspend, \u00a328k central budget underspend","quote":"At the end of Quarter 1 there was an overall projected overspend against the original budget for the year of approximately \u00a3878k. The overspend was primarily due to loss of rental income from the vacant Redhill Distribution Centre. The Property team were actively seeking new tenants.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Housing Delivery on Council Owned Car Parks FINAL","paper_url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s43457/43457.pdf","headline":"Funding for feasibility and business case work is being drawn from the Feasibility Studies (Capital Schemes) Reserve, not from revenue or borrowing.","detail":"Para 9 specifies that 'Funding from the Feasibility Studies (Capital Schemes) Reserve, be used to complete the necessary work to progress the preferred option for each car park.' This suggests capital investment in exploratory work is being funded from reserves rather than from operating revenue or new borrowing.","category":"reserves","matters":"Drawdown from capital reserves for exploratory work (advisers, feasibility studies, business cases) ahead of final decisions. Lender needs to understand the state of this reserve and whether funds are available for other capital priorities.","figures":"Not specified; amount to be determined","quote":"Funding from the Feasibility Studies (Capital Schemes) Reserve, be used to complete the necessary work to progress the preferred option for each car park","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Housing Delivery on Council Owned Car Parks FINAL","paper_url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s43457/43457.pdf","headline":"All disposals exceeding \u00a3100,000 require approval from East Surrey shadow authority under section 24 Direction, creating dependency during local government reorganisation.","detail":"Para 49 states the council 'is unable to declare the Site surplus to requirements currently and agree to dispose of the asset without referral back to Executive for decision and subsequently to East Surrey Council's approval under section 24.' All decisions must be referred to the shadow authority. This adds a further gating condition to project execution at a time of significant organisational change.","category":"governance","matters":"Execution risk in a period of reorganisation. The shadow authority's approval is a prerequisite for disposal; non-approval could block the entire project or cause delays that affect timing of cash flows.","figures":"\u00a3100,000 (s24 Direction threshold for referral)","quote":"the Council is unable to declare the Site surplus to requirements currently and agree to dispose of the asset without referral back to Executive for decision and subsequently to East Surrey Council's approval under section 24","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-24"},"name":"Reigate and Banstead","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Key projects workstream downgraded to Amber in LGR programme","lead":"Deteriorating status on critical LGR preparation activity suggests potential delays in restructuring planning, which could have knock-on effects on service delivery and the council's financial position during transition.","also":["43 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee on 2026-10-08","n_findings":44,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"O&amp;S Minute 28 Q1 Performance 2026-27","top_paper_url":"https://reigate-banstead.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s43581/43581.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":111,"news_drafts_total":2}}